---
source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Draft a new email or refine an existing local draft with LLM assistance

Usage: mxr draft [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  refine  Refine an existing local draft
  eval    Replay your most recent replies: draft each one from what was known just before you replied and compare it with what you sent (greeting, sign-off, length, invented numbers). Calls your LLM once per reply; nothing is saved or sent. Uses --account when given
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --to <TO>              Recipient email for a new draft
      --purpose <PURPOSE>    Plain-language purpose for a new draft
      --account <ACCOUNT>    Account key, email, or id
      --register <REGISTER>  Register to use when recipient has no relationship profile [possible values: casual, neutral, formal]
      --length <LENGTH>      Desired length [possible values: short, medium, long]
      --format <FORMAT>      [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]
  -h, --help                 Print help
